  "headword": "{摂|と}る",
  "reading": "とる",
  "romaji": "toru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to take in; to consume (nutrients, food)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to take in; to ingest; to consume (food, nutrients, sleep)",
      "explanation": "To take something into the body, especially nutrients, food, water, or sleep. This kanji spelling distinguishes it from other verbs read とる; it often appears in health and nutrition contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29372_toru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{栄養|えいよう}を{摂|と}る。",
      "english": "To take in nutrition.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29372_toru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{水分|すいぶん}をこまめに{摂|と}りましょう。",
      "english": "Let's take in fluids frequently.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29372_toru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{忙|いそが}しくても、{朝食|ちょうしょく}はしっかり{摂|と}るようにしている。",
      "english": "Even when I'm busy, I make sure to eat a proper breakfast.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive; the thing consumed is marked with を. Common objects are {栄養|えいよう} (nutrition), {水分|すいぶん} (fluids), カロリー (calories), {食事|しょくじ} (a meal), and {睡眠|すいみん} (sleep).\n\nThis is one of several verbs read とる. {摂|と}る is reserved for taking nutrients, food, or sleep into the body. For grabbing or picking up objects use {取|と}る, and the general kana spelling とる covers all of these readings in casual writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {栄養|えいよう}を{摂|と}る: to take in nutrition\n- {水分|すいぶん}を{摂|と}る: to stay hydrated\n- {睡眠|すいみん}を{摂|と}る: to get sleep",
